# muon_movie_quad.loop -- body of the /control/loop in macros/muon_movie_quad.mac.
#
# {endTime} is the loop variable (head time, ns).  tailRange / frameDir /
# frameStem are /control/alias values set in muon_movie_quad.mac.  The window is
# [endTime - tailRange, endTime]; segments fade with age over that width, giving
# the comet tail.  The front buffer is re-rendered, then read back to an EPS
# frame (printMode pixmap does a glReadPixels) with an auto-incremented index.
# The step is constant across the whole sweep (hard-capped, no phase change).
/vis/viewer/set/timeWindow/endTime {endTime} ns {tailRange} ns
/vis/viewer/refresh
/vis/ogl/export {frameDir}/{frameStem}
